The GUI textures in mixins/roughlyenoughitems/sprites.rs are REI's own
(runtime/src/main/resources/assets/roughlyenoughitems/textures/gui, MIT),
converted to runs of pixels by tools/sprites.mjs. Buttons use the game's own
button sprites in the light theme, REI's dark twins in the dark one.

This port rewrites REI's entry list, favorites, display history, search
grammar, recipe screen (with the tag category and the choose-page popup), its
config screen and the default plugin's categories in Rust for Horizon's native
mod API, from the game's own item and recipe tables. Changes from the original:
no plugin API (Horizon has no Java mods to register categories); the "+" button
moves crafting recipes only; the information category and the input methods are
not ported. The config screen shows every option REI shows; those whose part of
REI is not ported (the composite recipe screen, panel boundaries, category and
entry filtering, collapsible-entry editing, inventory search, the vanilla
recipe book and effects switches, cheat grabbing, the performance and debug
screens) keep their defaults and cannot be changed. It is not affiliated with
shedaniel, Mojang or Microsoft.
